  "_comment": "Soft lease limit on the 8-slot shared KV pool. In phase2_lease_kvu, leasing 6 of 8 slots gave the best task latency vs the main line (P50 -23%, P95 -21%) but new-task TTFT P95 +52%; leasing 8 kept TTFT level (+7%) at P50 -15%, P95 -16%, because more tasks decoding at once slows every token. lease_kvu8_soft6 leases up to 8 slots but admits new tasks only while fewer than 6 are busy or held, unless the oldest new task has waited 2 s: it should keep c6's tail and cap first-step waits near 2 s. W1 0.95X, seeds 42-44, each seed's four runs back to back. 12 runs, ~3 h. Check scheduler_summary: soft_held_back and overflow_admits show how often the limit bound. Compare with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_lease_soft --baseline fifo_c6_p5_cram4g; and --baseline lease_kvu8_c6.",
